Z||000003||theogre||11-10-2000||06:35 PM||||Maybe if you bothered to check the ecm codes..... Could be any number of things getting hot and puking.||||reg||1
Z||000004||strdream||11-10-2000||07:04 PM||||Find the ALDL (Assembly Line Diagnostic Link) connector, looking straight into it you will see two rows of pockets and that most of the ports are empty but there will be two terminals side by side in either the upper right corner or the lower left corner. With the key off use a paper clip or some other conductor and jumper these two teminals togather.  Now turn the key on engine NOT running and watch the CEL (Check Engine Light). it will flash long and short flashes. It is giveing you the trouble codes.  It will repeat each number three times and start the sequence over. When you have them writen down turn the key off and remove the jumper. post your results someone will have some advise for you. Maybe even me.<BR>Ross      ||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||11-11-2000||03:45 PM||||Check your fuel pressure. ||||reg||1
